WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:03.149
Hey youtubers, what’s up.

00:00:03.149 --> 00:00:08.160
There’s a brand new Avengers Trailer tonight
so just for fun I wanted to do my TOP 5 Ultron

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.160
Stories.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.740
There are a few key changes the movie is making
to his backstory as well as the Vision but

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.089
I’ll talk more about that when I post my
trailer video later tonight.

00:00:15.089 --> 00:00:16.090
This is all about the comics.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.590
So just to start my list off let’s say Number
5 is The First Appearance of Ultron in the

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:21.590
comics.

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:24.990
In case you haven’t read any of the old
Avengers Comics, the character was created

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.730
by Roy Thomas back in 1968.

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:32.290
The core concept and design of the character
were inspired by the living robot character

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:36.560
Makino from a Saturday Morning Serial from
the 1950s called Captain Video.

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:41.180
I love the idea that Saturday Morning Cartoons
inspired the creation of Ultron.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:47.100
George Lucas also borrowed a lot from Flash
Gordon Serials of the 50s when he wrote Star

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.100
Wars.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:49.720
it just melts your pop culture brain.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:56.670
So Ultron’s first appearance was Avengers
54 but that was just a cameo.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:02.210
It was actually a weird Masters of Evil story
where Ultron secretly hypnotizes Edwin Jarvis,

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:05.150
the Jarvis that we’re seeing in Agent Carter
right now.

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:09.840
He hypnotizes Jarvis into hiring the Masters
of Evil to take down the Avengers.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.154
Already you can see how there’s no way they
could turn this story into a movie.

00:01:13.154 --> 00:01:14.990
But the evolution of Ultron and everything
that came after with The Vision gets so much

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:23.250
more awesome when you think about Paul Bettany
playing Vision in the movie.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:27.100
Even cooler, that original Ultron story also
featured Black Panther and did a flashback

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.870
scene of how Uylesses Klaw tried to steal
all of Wakanda’s Vibranium.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:35.880
There’s a theory that’s who Andy Serkis
is playing in the movie and they’ll use

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:39.030
it to lay the groundwork for Black Panther
showing up in Civil War.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:47.180
So even though the movie is doing a modified
version of a very different Avengers comic

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.180
book story.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:52.920
It still has the DNA of Ultron’s very first
appearance in the 60s.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.270
It wasn’t till later in Avengers Issue 58
that they told the story of how Hank Pym created

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:02.320
Ultron using his own brainwaves as a template,
Ultron develops an Oedipal Complex, thinks

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.000
of Pym as his father and falls in love with
Janet Van Dyne.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.000
The Wasp.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:11.430
When he appeared in the previous issue he
revealed he was Ultron Version 5 and everyone

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.230
was like WTF happened to the other Four Versions.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:18.359
Again, some tweaks to this happening in the
movie that I’ll explain in my trailer video

00:02:18.359 --> 00:02:19.359
tonight.

00:02:19.359 --> 00:02:23.889
But Ultron is an evolving hypermind with the
emotional fortitude of an emo teenager.

00:02:23.889 --> 00:02:29.659
Which makes him by default, everyone’s worst
nightmare.

00:02:29.659 --> 00:02:31.900
Number 4 - The First Appearance of The Vision

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:35.049
I’m not talking about the original Vision,
this character here.

00:02:35.049 --> 00:02:37.859
This version was an alien from an alternate
dimension.

00:02:37.859 --> 00:02:42.629
During the 1960s Stan Lee decided he wanted
an Android character to join the Avengers

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:43.629
as a superhero.

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:45.989
Because they owned the rights to that original
Vision character, Stan Lee re-wrote him as

00:02:45.989 --> 00:02:47.020
the Android Vision.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:51.810
So when we talk about Vision in the context
of the Marvel Universe, we’re really talking

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:54.500
about the Second version.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:58.909
His first appearance was in 1968 in Avengers
57.

00:02:58.909 --> 00:03:03.010
The core of the story is about Vision being
more of a synthetic human than an android.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:05.980
It’s part of the character’s journey that
he endeavors to be human.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:10.159
It’s like Data on Star Trek Next Gen, it’s
like Pinnochio.

00:03:10.159 --> 00:03:13.159
Which makes you think even more about the
“strings” line from the first Trailer

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:17.819
and Ultron as a dark version of pinocchio.

00:03:17.819 --> 00:03:22.180
The Avengers learn that Ultron 5 created Vision
to infiltrate their team and destroy them.

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:27.180
But he made Vision so perfectly, that he begins
to feel emotions, develops a conscience and

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.779
turns against Ultron.

00:03:28.779 --> 00:03:32.919
If any of you are Breaking Bad fans or Watchmen
fans, at the end of this story after Vision

00:03:32.919 --> 00:03:37.050
and the Avengers defeat Ultron, Stan Lee wrote
in the Ozymandius poem as an epilogue.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:41.230
It’s a poem about a traveler who goes to
Egypt and sees this inscription written by

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:42.290
an ancient King of a great empire.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:46.689
And the inscription basically says, look at
how awesome I am.

00:03:46.689 --> 00:03:50.099
But the traveler can only see miles and miles
of sand in every direction.

00:03:50.099 --> 00:03:56.030
Everything the ancient king claimed to have
built had crumbled to dust.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:59.139
In the context of the Avengers story, Ultron
is the ancient king.

00:03:59.139 --> 00:04:01.889
But if you think about it in the context of
the movie.

00:04:01.889 --> 00:04:05.359
Tony Stark is the ancient king.

00:04:05.359 --> 00:04:08.063
And Ultron played by James Spader, is going
to crush everything he’s tried to build.

00:04:08.063 --> 00:04:09.063
In a very literal way.

00:04:09.063 --> 00:04:13.310
At least until the Paul Bettany Vision comes
along and crushes Ultron’s empire.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:23.200
So I guess at the end of the day, the movie
version of Ultron is still Ozymandias.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:27.680
Way later in the comics, in Avengers #93 there’s
this Journey to the Center of the Earth story

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:31.620
where Ant Man shrinks down and goes inside
The Vision’s body to examine him.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:37.130
That lays the teaser that the Vision’s body
was created from the original human torch.

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:41.889
But they didn’t fully explore that idea
till Avengers #134.

00:04:41.889 --> 00:04:49.039
Ultron Story Number 3 - We Stand At Armageddon

00:04:49.039 --> 00:04:51.650
This was Avengers Number 66 through 68.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.870
It was the introduction of Adamantium in the
Marvel Universe.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:56.690
The Vision, under the control of Ultron.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:00.161
Tries to steal Adamantium from the Avengers
so that he can upgrade his body and become

00:05:00.161 --> 00:05:01.161
indestructible.

00:05:01.161 --> 00:05:06.250
A scientist named Myron Maclain accidentaly
invented it while trying to create a new indestructibe

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:08.410
alloy for the US Military.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.280
Wakanda gives him a small portion of Vibranium.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.789
And after a lot of experimenting.

00:05:13.789 --> 00:05:15.340
Adamantium is born.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:19.430
The writers made it so that the scientist
didn’t fully understand what he did to create

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:21.300
the adamantium, it was billed as an accident.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.720
I think just to keep the Avengers from getting
overpowered.

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:28.229
I mean, if you can make an unlimited supply
of adamantium, why not use it to make everything

00:05:28.229 --> 00:05:30.440
that needs metal.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:34.000
Adamantium cars, Adamantium refrigerator.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:38.080
Because of the rights issues, the Marvel Movies
have stuck with Vibranium as it’s only super

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.080
strong metal.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:44.419
So I’m interested to see how Ultron seeks
it out for his final body.

00:05:44.419 --> 00:05:46.720
Number 2 - Ultron Unlimited

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:53.069
This is from the 1998 Avengers Run #19 to
22 by Kurt Busiek.

00:05:53.069 --> 00:05:58.259
Ultron takes over the Western European country
of Slorenia and turns everyone into Ultron

00:05:58.259 --> 00:05:59.259
clones.

00:05:59.259 --> 00:06:00.849
It’s a robot Hitler story.

00:06:00.849 --> 00:06:06.419
This was a way darker telling of the Ultron
Mythos.

00:06:06.419 --> 00:06:09.750
Instead of threatening genocide, he actually
goes through with it.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:17.689
And Hank Pym, his creator, has to live knowing
that his creation killed an entire country

00:06:17.689 --> 00:06:19.169
of people.

00:06:19.169 --> 00:06:22.699
Look at this panel here, doesn’t this look
familiar.

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:24.850
This is the promo art for the movie.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:29.219
And the country the Avengers go to is called
Sokovia.

00:06:29.219 --> 00:06:33.479
Sounds a lot like the Slorenia of the comic
story.

00:06:33.479 --> 00:06:36.719
And my Number 1 story - Anhiliation Conquest

00:06:36.719 --> 00:06:39.120
This kind of dovetails with the Ultron Imperative
Storyline.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.219
So I guess I’ll mention them both.

00:06:43.219 --> 00:06:47.280
In the wake of Civil War, Iron Man as a character
came off as kind of a bad guy.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:51.830
So to make him more sympathetic to audiences,
Bendis had Ultron infect Tony Stark’s Extremis

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:52.830
Armor.

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:56.520
Because extremis is bonded with Tony Stark’s
DNA, Ultron essentially takes control of Tony

00:06:56.520 --> 00:07:01.800
Stark and goes on to create a new body that
ends up looking like Janet Van Dyne, albiet

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:04.259
with Metal skin.

00:07:04.259 --> 00:07:09.150
Eventually Ares defeats Ultron and shoots
his disembodied consciousness into deep space.

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:11.830
Then in the Annhiliation Conquest storyline.

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:15.240
Ultron’s consciousness finds the Phalanx
and becomes their new god.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:18.290
He uses them to try an conquer the galaxy.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:25.610
That conflict is the call to action that causes
the new Guardians of The Galaxy to form.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:28.120
The team that serves as the basis for the
Guardians Movie.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:34.289
So Ultron is responsible for the creation
of the Guardians of the Galaxy in the comics.

00:07:34.289 --> 00:07:39.659
It’s totally possible that at the end of
Avengers 2, they shoot him into deep space

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:42.560
and he shows up as the main villain of Guardians
of the Galaxy 2.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:48.520
We’ll have to ask James Gunn about that.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:51.920
Really I’m not expecting that to happen,
but it is possible if he wants to go with

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:53.279
something straight out of the comics.

00:07:53.279 --> 00:07:57.770
Here’s my big question for you guys, what
is your favorite Ultron story from the comics?

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:01.499
And do you think it’s something they could
realistically do in a future movie.

00:08:01.499 --> 00:08:05.240
Ultron seems like he might end up being a
Red Skull type villain.

00:08:05.240 --> 00:08:09.449
Someone really epic but only shows up once
every 6 or 7 years in the movies.

00:08:09.449 --> 00:08:11.539
I really don’t think we’ll see Ultron
again in Infinity War.

00:08:11.539 --> 00:08:15.290
I think they’ll probably simplify things
and just have Thanos leading an army of Kree

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:16.720
or something similar.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:20.550
Some other galactic race that isn’t controlled
by FOX or Sony.

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:23.479
In related news, new trailer for Avengers
2 tonight.

